    "title": "Thousands of popular infant car seats recalled over a safety concern parents can’t ignore",
    "text": "NewsGraco SnugRide Turn & Slide RecallGracoGraco is recalling a select number of SnugRide Turn & Slide infant products after identifying a structural issue during a post-production laboratory test, the company said. The recall involves SnugRide Turn & Slide products sold in the U.S. from January 2026 through March 2026 at Amazon, Babylist, Target, Walmart and online at GracoBaby.com. “We know parents rely on Graco products every day, and we understand this may create frustration and disruption for families. We are working quickly to support affected families and will provide a replacement product at no cost,” Graco said in the recall notice. Which products are recalled?The recall applies to the following SnugRide Turn & Slide products with color names and model numbers for reference: SnugRide Turn & Slide Rotating Infant Car SeatColors and Model numbers: Noir / Black: 2231809Sandstone / Tan: 2231885Mulberry / Girl-Plum: 2231806Noir / Black: 2231881Noir / Black: 2231884SnugRide Turn & Slide Rotating Infant Car Seat BaseColor and Model Number:Black: 2231810Modes Nest Travel System with SnugRide Turn & Slide ICSColor and Model Number:Noir / Black: 2243083No other Graco car seats are affected by the recall, including EasyTurn and Turn2Me. No other SnugRide models are included in the recall. How do I know if my product is included?1. Check the product images on Graco’s recall page to confirm that you have a SnugRide Turn & Slide product. 2. Look at the model number on the product label.3. Enter the model number on the Graco recall page. 4. Enter the serial number to confirm your product details. The serial number is the five digit number listed on the label directly below the Date of Manufacture. What consumers should doConsumers should immediately stop using the recalled seat with the base. Graco said the seat may be used without the base while you wait for a replacement product. Remove the seat from the base and find the label showing the model number, date of manufacture and serial number. Upload a photo of the white label found on the base to Graco’s recall page.Register for the recall using the Graco registration form and select your replacement option. Do not return the recalled product to a store. Diane Mwai is a trending news reporter for AL.com from Birmingham, Alabama. Diane covers recalls, consumer warnings, settlements, tech company layoffs and more. She has previously covered social media, breaking...",
